  "rendered": {
    "title": "Pay-per-call x402 LLM endpoint lands with hardened billing",
    "intro": "Today's nightly opens up an x402-protected public chat completions endpoint, letting external clients pay per request to talk to Aura's models. A follow-up tightens how the server connects to the z-billing service so usage settlement can't be pointed at unsafe URLs.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "9:25 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-09T04:25:43.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-09T04:25:43.000Z",
        "title": "x402-paid public chat completions endpoint",
        "summary": "Aura's server now exposes an x402-protected public LLM router so third-party clients can pay per request to call hosted models, with full configuration over price, models, network, and facilitator.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added `POST /api/public/x402/v1/chat/completions` and `GET /api/public/x402/v1/models` as a new public surface, implementing the x402 protocol directly at the Axum boundary since reference middleware only targets TS/Go/Python.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Defaults to the `upto` x402 scheme on Base Sepolia USDC with a $0.02 per-request ceiling, settling actual token usage against z-billing quotes via the new `LlmUsageQuote` client path.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Operators can tune the endpoint through a new env surface — `AURA_X402_PAY_TO`, `AURA_X402_CHAT_PRICE`, `AURA_X402_MODELS`, `AURA_X402_MAX_TOKENS`, `AURA_X402_FACILITATOR_URL`, `AURA_X402_NETWORK`, and related knobs — documented in the README.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Request handling enforces guardrails for paid traffic: max 64 messages, 32k chars per message, 64k total, a configurable `max_tokens` cap, and a 120s default completion timeout.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "8:40 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-09T15:40:50.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-09T15:40:50.000Z",
        "title": "Billing client rejects unsafe service URLs",
        "summary": "The z-billing client now validates its configured base URL before issuing any request, closing off SSRF-style misconfigurations against the new x402 settlement path.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Service URLs are now parsed and joined through `url::Url` instead of string concatenation, and must be HTTPS pointing at a public host; HTTP loopback is allowed only in debug/test builds.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "46c9194757af4ce7cc4d823487bdc5278df6d3f6"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Private, loopback, link-local, broadcast, unspecified, and `localhost`-style hosts are rejected, as are URLs that embed userinfo, surfaced through a new `BillingError::InsecureServiceUrl` and `InvalidServiceUrl` errors.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "46c9194757af4ce7cc4d823487bdc5278df6d3f6"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "New x402 public LLM endpoint with on-chain micropayments",
      "Billing client now rejects insecure or private service URLs",
      "Configurable model allowlist, price ceiling, and facilitator for x402"
    ],
    "raw_commit_count": 3
  }
